  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "1 \u00b7 Remote access and execution",
      "items": [
        "Human IAM authorizes the SSM tunnel. SSM Agent starts the connection; no inbound EC2 ports or public IP are needed.",
        "Gateway and Kiro CLI / Codex / Claude Code execute on EC2. Independent laptop agents remain outside this service."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "2 \u00b7 Policy and credentials",
      "items": [
        "* Proposed privileged sync reads S3 through a gateway endpoint and writes a protected file:// policy source. File and ancestor directories must be unwritable by Crew.",
        "Keep the EC2 instance role narrow. MCP caller identity / tool grants and downstream task-role IAM are separate controls."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "3 \u00b7 Evidence and deployment scope",
      "items": [
        "CloudTrail records SSM API activity, not forwarded payload. Application collectors supply tool evidence; a Logs endpoint supports private delivery.",
        "Egress routes need firewall enforcement; NAT alone does not filter. Optional MCP services need equivalent controls for external calls.",
        "Retained nightly: 0.7.0.dev20260911060948 \u00b7 fa0d8cf3c241. Architecture proposal; deployment and integration are untested."
      ]
    }
  ]
